<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernardo O'Higgins</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1778">1778</a>–<a href="/years/1842">1842</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernardo O'Higgins was a leader of Chilean independence and the son of an Irish-born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a> he defeated the royalists at Chacabuco in 1817 and Maipú in 1818. As Supreme Director he signed Chile's declaration of independence in 1818, but his authoritarian rule led to his resignation in 1823.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernardo-ohiggins.jpg" alt="Bernardo O'Higgins" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Gil de Castro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ohiggins.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
